  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "I live in Australia, which means usually when I am up and ready to update my world there are usually a fair amount of people in an instance, so I usually wait until the world dies down before I update so that they have plenty of time to enjoy the world with friends before it disappears for a day, or two considering that I miss the public approval hours. \n\nI used to use web panels to tell people what's happening when they happen but since it's been disabled I don't have any other way to warn people of impending updates. I would love the ability to send UI messages to people in the world to tell them when I'm updating or telling them about events, plans etc. \n\nObviously this could be abused but I'm pretty sure it'd be easy to have a cooldown timer (people who make  public worlds tend to not be malicious enough to circumvent stuff like that).",
